      "claim": "The posterior distribution is proportional to the product of the likelihood and prior: P(θ|X₁,...,Xₙ) ∝ ∏ᵢ=1ⁿ P(Xᵢ|θ) × Prior(θ)",
      "supported": true,
      "evidence_or_problem": "Source: [00:33:37\u201300:34:13] 'So like if a function looks like this, so this is just a product of P of Xi given theta, since all of our observations are independent and identically distributed, we multiply it by prior distribution and we renormalize it according to Bayes' theorem.'"
